   "pull_request": {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/pulls/7413",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/pull/7413",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/pull/7413.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/pull/7413.patch",
    "merged_at": null
   },
   "body": "When a URL contains path parameters delimited by semicolons (e.g. `https://musicbrainz.org/ws/2/artist;name=Nirvana`), `urllib.parse.urlparse` splits the path into `.path` and `.params` attributes. `HTTPDigestAuth.build_digest_header()` was only using `.path` and `.query`, so the `uri` field in the `Authorization` header was truncated, causing authentication to fail on servers that validate the full request URI.\n\nThis was reported in #6990 with a concrete MusicBrainz API example.\n\nFix: include `p_parsed.params` when reconstructing the path in `build_digest_header()`.\n\nAdded a unit test that verifies the `uri` field includes semicolon-delimited path parameters.",
   "closed_by": null,
